[Music]  okay everyone so this is my spoiler free  review of the latest james bond  installment no time to die this is the  last film daniel craig is doing as the  notorious james bond i was fortunate  enough to be invited to a screening for  this  and i got to see it on imax and what i  had done before this film is binge watch  all of the james bond films today on  craig beforehand to be prepared  one i'm really happy i did that because  there is a lot in this movie that throws  back especially to the last film but  stuff even that throws back to casino  royale so make sure you refresh on these  films in particular spectre you really  gotta refresh because there's a lot  tying into that which actually  surprising but i do think works i think  what this film does really well is tie  up previous plot lines that were left  loose from other james bond films and  kind of honored the whole series with  daniel craig as a whole and let it have  a nice bow here  i went into this film with literally no  expectations because for me with the  daniel craig films it's been like you  know casino royale really good then  quantum soul is not so great and sky  fall amazing and then spectre was like  eh  so but i you know you had to think like  okay something's got to give because  it's kind of in every other film for  daniel craig here that's successful  and really good and then it happened  again where with no time to die i was so  impressed with this movie um what i was  most excited about was kerry joji  fukunaga  directing this thing because i loved how  he did true detective season one he's a  talented director it was interesting to  see him do something in a big budget  film like this and he doesn't disappoint  this was the best paced bond film to me  it was the only bond film out of the  bunch with daniel craig that i didn't  feel bored in any points  it was two hours and 45 minutes that  felt like an hour and a half to me and  what kerry does so well as a director  here is he  just keeps it moving but every single  action sequence is so well thought out  to make it unique and different than  typical bond action sequences and it has  the best opening sequence of any bond  films  hands down and i argue out of this  daniel craig saga here that it has the  best third act out of any of those films  so  where i would compare it to is my  favorite was skyfall but what i thought  this is better than skyfall was that  i wasn't crazy about the third act of  skyfall and i thought it really slowed  down and got boring but this didn't feel  that at all i felt like the whole movie  i was on the edge of my seat really into  it and what was most important was the  focal point of this film was that it  would give daniel craig a nice emotional  send-off and it does go there people  will be emotional with this film and  that was such an important payoff when  you're closing out when people get so  attached to an actor who's playing james  bond that you give him a rifle send off  that gives him enough time now you're  gonna see  things about this film that weren't so  great even though i'm praising it so  much was that rami malek  he's great but  his character is underwritten a bit so  it's not gonna go down really is a  historic bond villain he's very paper  thin but he does a great job and he's  fun to watch on the screen and another  thing was it's bittersweet because on a  day armas  literally  is amazing in this film like scene  stealer but she's not in the film really  that much at all so you're like at one  point like  where is she like  this was someone who just was amazing  and apart and there's it's bizarre how  little she is in this movie so that was  a big complaint of mine but going to the  positives again han zimmer doing the  score this time around amazing and he  does cool things with classic bond  themes so i really appreciate that and  he really is another point to why you  feel kind of pumped up during this movie  and  it has twists that are successfully  landed here that you don't really see  coming and  again i think that it's the perfect  movie for it's gonna sound corny saying  this but like you could take your dad  and mom to this and they're not gonna be  confused they're gonna enjoy it just as  much as you do it is truly a successful  entertaining action flick and if you're  not really into a lot of action  you know this isn't really the bond for  you and  it really is centered on how great the  action sequences are plus getting again  big character emotional payoffs for  daniel craig and james bond  now  i was  a little disappointed in the humor  there's very little humor in this film  so  the wit's supposed to be taken down with  daniel craig anyway as james bond that's  not really his forte as james bond but  here it could have used a little more  humor it doesn't even really try and  that's surprising is you got phoebe  waller's bridge here who is great with  sharp wit writing on this thing you  don't really kind of feel her script  writing come out in this besides that  though again the new characters you're  gonna like the old characters get enough  screen time that you're happy about it  and it's  really just  an exciting  big  tentpole movie to come out when it's  desperately needed for theaters at the  moment and i think it will be divisive  though for die hard bond fans i think  some people are going to be  maybe not as into the plot as you would  expect but it got me but i could see why  some wouldn't and i don't want to spoil  anything so i won't go in that too much  detail but you know lower expectations  you're going to see a lot of reviews  praising it today including mine i'm  giving this thing a 9.2 it's my favorite  bond filling by the daniel craig bunch  but i could totally see the argument for  skyfall or christina royale being your  favorite over this one it's close like  it's so you could flip it back and forth  like it's just gonna be kind of  remembered in that tier of those three  bond films of craig and we can kind of  forget about quantum souls and spectre  but i'm happy that it's not in that  other bottom tier with those two and  that it's going to be remembered in that  and i think people are just going to  debate between skyfall casino royale and  no time to die and i think either  argument is valid i don't think it's  like so much better in my opinion than  skyfall which is my favorite i think  it's a little better so i'm happy and  that's great to end a series of five  movies on that for daniel craig and it  leaves you excited for where this is  going to go next so when you see the  film let me know what you think comment  below and let me know if you plan on  seeing and let me know your thoughts  just in general about the bond films  that have come out down craig and if you  like them or not i'd love to hear your  thoughts on that as well oh and also i  want to mention love billy eilish's song  here in the opening credits the opening  credits sequence is really good too so  you won't be disappointed with that as  well so please follow me at steverlyshow  on twitter and instagram for more of me  and if you really like what i do here  please subscribe so you don't miss one  of my reviews i do movie reviews tv  reviews i also do celebrating videos as  well so you want to check that out and  i'll see you next time

